  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The edge of this axe has never been sharpened. Smiths who look closely say that it has no edge at all, only a line where the steel stops, and that the line is thinner than anything they know how to grind.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p><strong>Sundering Sweep.</strong> Once per day, as an action, you swing the axe through a 15-foot Cone. Each creature in it makes a [[/save ability=dex dc=20 format=long]], taking [[/damage 8d12 type=slashing]] damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. Walls, doors and other objects in the Cone take the full damage. The axe regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>The Cut That Stays.</strong> A thing this axe has split cannot be joined again by any craft or magic short of a wish: a gate, a chain, a crown, or a border stone. Smiths can tell at a glance that a break was made by it.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
